  "body": "**Blocked by:** #500\n\n## Context\n\n`docs/adr/2026-09-24-choke-point-composed-from-domain-modules.md` (added by #500) records a lint cap of 900 lines per production source file, so no module can grow the way `backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/chokePoint.ts` did. #529 applies it to `backend/`, and this issue applies it to `web/`. The largest production file in `web/src` today, `web/src/views/mailbox/MailboxClient.tsx`, has about 885 lines.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd `max-lines: [\"error\", { max: 900, skipBlankLines: true, skipComments: true }]` to `web/eslint.config.js` for `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`, excluding `**/*.test.{ts,tsx}` and `**/__tests__/**`. Next to the rule, add a comment pointing to the ADR and saying why tests are exempt.\n\nDo not add any per-file exemption. If a production file exceeds 900 counted lines when you implement this, do not raise the cap and do not exempt the file. Stop with `Relay-Step-Status: blocked` and name the file and its count.\n\n## Touches\n\n- web/eslint.config.js\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n- The rule and its comment.\n\n### Out of scope\n- `backend/` (#529).\n- Splitting any file.\n- Any other lint rule.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `pnpm run verify` in `web/` passes.\n- A production `.tsx` file of 901 counted lines fails `pnpm run lint` with `max-lines`, and a test file of the same size does not. Check this by hand once, revert it, and say so in the pull request description.\n- The config contains no `eslint-disable` and no per-file override for `max-lines`.\n",
